    "isDraft": false,
    "headRefOid": "17411f25a40b2b6927683475e4eb76ba62f47452",
    "title": "feat(tools): alternative qwen3_coder / qwen3_xml parsers behind a switch",
    "url": "https://github.com/1CatAI/1Cat-vLLM/pull/1446",
    "body": "> **Note for reviewers:** the two `*_120_*.py` implementations are large (about 7.4k lines) and their comments and docstrings are currently in Chinese. The switch mechanism, the env registration and the `__init__.py` changes are in English. If you would rather review this as English-commented code, say so and I will translate before you spend time on it.\n\n## Motivation\n\nAdds an alternative implementation of the two Qwen3 tool parsers, selectable at import time:\n\n```bash\nVLLM_TOOL_PARSER_IMPL=120   # default -> *_120_tool_parser.py\nVLLM_TOOL_PARSER_IMPL=150   # upstream parsers\n```\n\nThe two are independent modules and the switch only picks a class in the `tool_parsers` registry, so nothing is overwritten. **Taking only the switch mechanism is supported**: delete the `*_120_*.py` modules and leave the variable at its `\"150\"` default. That alone may be the useful part if you have your own parser work in flight.\n\n## Why a parallel implementation rather than a patch series\n\nThe upstream parsers are large and were rewritten substantially — on the order of 73% new code, a different approach (balanced-delimiter matching upstream versus escape scanning here), and almost no shared function names. A series of point fixes reaches \"the function exists\" but not \"the state machine agrees\"; a pointwise port stalled at 15 of 23 conformance cases.\n\n## What the alternative implementation adds\n\n- **True incremental streaming** of tool-call arguments, with per-call JSON and XML routing and configurable granularity.\n- **Streaming anchors**: partial output can be emitted before the call body is complete.\n- **A 0-5 fix ladder** (`VLLM_QWEN3X_TOOL_FIX`) covering parsing failures bisected during bring-up. Level 0 behaves like upstream, so it can be turned off piecemeal.\n- **`tool_choice=\"none\"` intent detection.** When a client expresses \"do not call the tool\" in prose rather than in the field, the request is the only signal available — the model cannot see `tool_choice` at all (the first 12 generated token ids are identical for `auto` and `none`).\n- **Deferral of non-whitelisted calls while thinking is enabled**, so tag-shaped text quoted inside the reasoning block is not treated as a real call. (Finish-time emission for those calls is in #1443.)\n\n## A note on the Chinese text\n\nThe matching patterns and some error strings in the implementation are Chinese **by design**: they match Chinese user prompts and are part of the behaviour, not documentation. Translating them would change what the parser accepts.\n\n## Testing\n\nConformance suite of 37 cases covering streaming and non-streaming tool calls, multiple calls per response, nested arguments, mixed text and calls, and the fixed regressions from the ladder levels. `VLLM_TOOL_PARSER_IMPL=150` on the same suite produces the upstream results unchanged.",
